{
  "suite": "followups_v2",
  "kind": "trajectory",
  "about": "Corpus v2, held out: follow-up turns that were not used to design the shadow FAST/DEEP router (brain/fastdeep_router.py). Staged in evals/scenarios_next/ until the user approves it; the freeze (python -m evals.fastdeep_v2 --freeze) moves it to evals/scenarios/ and records its fingerprint (docs/FAST_DEEP_V2_PROTOCOL.md). Subjects appear nowhere in the v1 corpus or the Stage B runs. Five groups, each scenario's 'group': A, confusion and re-explanation follow-ups, explicit and implicit; B, deepening follow-ups that are not confusion; C, follow-ups that should stay FAST (a value again, thanks, a remark, a correction, a topic shift); D, first-time explanations; E, a confusion follow-up and then a turn that should return to FAST. Modes are the rubric's existing ones, so the rubric fingerprint does not change.",
  "defaults": {
    "checks": {
      "not_searched": true,
      "no_cards": true
    }
  },
